{"id":255024243886138,"type":"artist","name":"Los Lobos","artist":null,"year":1973,"weight":38,"info":{"tags":["rock","latin","tex-mex","americana","spanish"],"country":"US","begin":"1973","kind":"Group","similar":["Latin Playboys","John Hiatt","Los Lonely Boys","Santana","Chuck Prophet","The J. Geils Band","Texas Tornados","Little Village","Bruce Springsteen","Big Head Todd and the Monsters"],"disambiguation":"Chicano rock band","img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/LosLobos.jpg?width=500","bio":"Los Lobos es una banda de rock, muy influenciada por el rock and roll, el tex-mex, la música country, el folk, el rhythm & blues, el blues, y la música tradicional española y mexicana, como los boleros y los norteños.\n\nLa banda surge en los años sesenta, su trabajo se centra en versionear éxitos del momento. Es a partir de los años setenta cuando comienzan a fusionar la música tradicional mexicana con los nuevos ritmos y sonidos rockeros"},"works":[{"id":7620901693067,"type":"album","name":"Just Another Band from East L.A.","artist":"Los Lobos","year":1977,"weight":4,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[{"name":"For the Record - The 70s","n":1}],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":212547025142174,"type":"album","name":"Sí se puede!","artist":"Los Lobos","year":1977,"weight":7,"yt":"JiZs4rz8ZDU","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":21247504317465,"name":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Tejano Music","rank":11,"scaruffi":null},{"id":130106164261830,"name":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Mexican Music","rank":178,"scaruffi":null},{"id":147676066674281,"name":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Texan Music","rank":156,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":3}},{"id":215895245114064,"type":"album","name":"Del este de Los Angeles (Just Another Band From East L.A.)","artist":"Los Lobos","year":1978,"weight":9,"yt":"sfpdejgOBpk","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":211801543514175,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Son jaroch