rcusión de Papa Dee Allen y el saxo de Harold Brown. Desde All Day Music (1971) arrasaron con «Slippin’ into Darkness», «The Cisco Kid», «Low Rider» y «Why Can’t We Be Friends?»: la vida en el paisaje urbano sombrío de Los Ángeles (como N.W.A. veinte años después), un ritmo abierto y terroso y el foco de la influencia latina en el funk, himnos de la cultura chicana del Suroeste. Fueron la banda con la que Hendrix tocó por última vez.","color":"#22c55e","family":"Bandas de funk de los setenta","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/#war"},{"id":227407993671548,"name":"Roots-rock de los ochenta y cow-punk","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1984,"end":1995,"desc":"Como en 1970 tras 1966, la new wave de 1976 va seguida de un revival del roots-rock, esta vez gradual y disfrazado: punks que desfiguran los estilos tradicionales (X, Dream Syndicate, Gun Club) y los «cow-punks» que tocan country ambientado entre inadaptados: Long Ryders, Jason & The Scorchers, Fetchin Bones, Lone Justice, Beat Farmers. El populismo de Los Lobos, Del Fuegos, Del-Lords y Walkabouts; en la Costa Oeste, los dementes Camper Van Beethoven, Donner Party, Catheads, Thin White Rope y los American Music Club de Mark Eitzel; en Texas, Wild Seeds, Poi Dog Pondering, Glass Eye; en los Grandes Lagos, BoDeans, Soul Asylum, Afghan Whigs, Shrimp Boat y los canadienses Cowboy Junkies. Nashville se renueva con los neotradicionalistas (George Strait, Randy Travis, Garth Brooks, Lyle Lovett, Steve Earle, Dwight Yoakam) y el surf instrumental vuelve con Shadowy Men On A Shadowy Planet.","color":"#f59e0b","family":"Raíces: rock'n'roll, country y roots","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#roots-80s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":97084934025145,"artist":"Los Lobos","artist_id":255024243886138,"title":"How Will The Wolf Survive","year":1984,"ess":0,"yt":"lJVsUMKftMo","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Roots-rock de los ochenta y cow-punk","scene_id":227407993671548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#roots-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.17"],"pages":[[1,191,null]]},{"id":224376794422375,"artist":"Los Lobos","artist_id":255024243886138,"title":"Shakin' Shakin' Shakes","year":1987,"ess":0,"yt":"CHO5iwzM8pc","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Roots-rock de los ochenta y cow-punk","scene_id":227407993671548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#roots-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.17"],"pages":[[1,191,null]]},{"id":78100753044664,"artist":"Los Lobos","artist_id":255024243886138,"title":"The Neighborhood","year":1990,"ess":0,"yt":"-wj9hNmrRoo","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Roots-rock de los ochenta y cow-punk","scene_id":227407993671548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#roots-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.17"],"pages":[[1,191,null]]},{"id":27948083654335,"artist":"Los Lobos","artist_id":255024243886138,"title":"Kiko","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"tYM9zBSYn2U","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Roots-rock de los ochenta y cow-punk","scene_id":227407993671548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#roots-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.17"],"pages":[[1,191,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":191,"text":"…and catchy mixture of cow-punk and folk-rock on Born in a Barn (Homestead, 1984). Populism 1984-86 The ultimate creature of Los Angeles' barrios, Los Lobos (2), recycled an exuberant combination of rhythm'n'blues and tex-mex, of Doug Sahm and Flaco Jimenez. How Will The Wolf Survive (1984) was possibly…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":191,"text":"…passages a` la Duke Ellington, cajun accordions, cumbia tempos, New Orleans' rhythm'n'blues, mandolin-driven polkas, boogie, funk and rock'n'roll. Los Lobos' caustic, fatalistic and nostalgic social melodrama had become the soundtrack of the American melting-pot and of the American dream. With Johnson…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Breakthrough with \"La Bamba\"","body":"While they had released albums and gained some attention earlier, Los Lobos' career truly took off after they recorded \"La Bamba\" for the 1987 movie about Richie Valens. \"But things really took off with what song? Of course, it was La Bamba. Loose Lobos recorded that song for the movie about Richie Valens' life which was released in 1987.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 25 - The Hispanic Influence on 70s Popular Music","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Formation","body":"Los Lobos was formed in 1973. \"Loose Lobos formed in 1973 and released their first album, Just Another Band, from East LA in 1977.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 25 - The Hispanic Influence on 70s Popular Music","url":null}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":212547025142174,"type":"album","name":"Sí se puede!","list_id":130106164261830,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Mexican Music","src":"musthear","rank":178,"year":1977,"note":null,"yt":"JiZs4rz8ZDU","scaruffi":null},{"id":212547025142174,"type":"album","name":"Sí se puede!","list_id":21247504317465,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Tejano Music","src":"musthear","rank":11,"year":1977,"note":null,"yt":"JiZs4rz8ZDU","scaruffi":null},{"id":212547025142174,"type":"album","name":"Sí se puede!","list_id":147676066674281,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Texan Music","src":"musthear","rank":156,"year":1977